WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:06.060
Dexter, the twisted tale of a serial killer
with a moral code, was a massive ratings hit

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:06.760
for Showtime.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:12.120
It was also an influential series that prompted
a slew of similarly lethal anti-heroes on

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:12.620
TV.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.160
Now it's time to conduct an autopsy on the
show's conclusion.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:22.000
When Dexter was just two years old, his mother
was brutally killed at the hands of a cartel

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.920
boss, and he and his brother were left sitting
in her blood.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.480
At first, the audience is encouraged to believe
that this foundational trauma is what put

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.160
Dexter down the path to being a serial killer.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:37.360
When Dexter's adopted father, Harry, realizes
his son lacks emotional empathy and might

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:42.560
possibly be a sociopath like when he finds
Dexter killing neighborhood pets he teaches

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.160
Dexter a code so the child won't get caught.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.540
"The code of Harry, my foster father, is satisfied."

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:52.400
But by the end of Dexter, his story is far
more complicated.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.680
As it turns out, it was a criminal psychiatrist
who had come up with the code.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.440
Harry was only responsible for teaching it
to Dexter, and it wasn't until Dexter's first

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.860
kill that he finally understood the monster
he'd helped create.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:09.960
It would be years before Dexter learned that
his father's death had been at his own hands,

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.320
once he'd realized what his adopted son was
capable of.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:18.600
One of the most compelling things about Dexter
is his incredible level of self-awareness.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:23.720
According to professionals, it's this introspection
that makes him an unrealistic psychopath,

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.280
in spite of being so relatable to viewers.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.020
He struggles in society, just as we all do.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:34.760
But in Dexter's case, he struggles with feeling
empathy and love, even though he understands

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:35.700
what it looks like.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:36.820
"Just like me.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:38.680
Empty inside."

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:44.280
As the narrative progresses from the beginning
to the end of Dexter, we see him go from someone

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:49.520
who must imitate human emotion to a man who
actually does feel and comes to truly care

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:50.860
about those closest to him.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:56.189
In fact, it's this emotional development that
causes Dexter to get so many people around

00:01:56.189 --> 00:01:57.340
him hurt or killed.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:02.340
In the anthology The Psychology of Dexter,
author Christopher Ryan writes:

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:06.940
"Dexter is both cold-blooded killer and warm-hearted
family man.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.740
Unfeeling assassin and supportive friend.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.240
Like all of us, he is confused, yet certain.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.220
He's the best and worst we can be often simultaneously."

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:23.379
Dexter's audience is so focused on what he'll
get away with next that a key aspect of the

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:24.740
show often gets overlooked.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.560
If America's criminal justice system actually
worked better, and criminals weren't set free

00:02:29.569 --> 00:02:34.180
by means of legal loopholes or skilled defense
attorneys, there would be no need for vigilantes

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:35.060
like Dexter.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:40.090
So when he sets his sights on unfairly freed
predators, Dexter is highlighting a real-life

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.080
crisis in America.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:45.400
And, in a way, his actions are making the
world a little bit safer for women and children.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:50.340
On the flip side, Dexter also shows us how
easy it is to game the law enforcement system

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.120
from the inside.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:56.500
Harry's code insists that the person Dexter
targets must be a killer or other kind of

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.760
confirmed monster.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.900
But since Dexter is able to change information
in a computer database, it only takes a few

00:03:02.909 --> 00:03:07.750
keystrokes to release someone as his own prey,
on the occasion he gets bored and needs a

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:08.240
victim.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:13.380
This system is how Dexter eventually identifies
the men responsible for his mother's death.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:18.919
And because of his easy-going persona, there
are few people who ever strongly suspect something

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:23.360
is off with Dexter, at least until much later
on in his story.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:29.200
Harry's code defines Dexter's approach to
vigilante justice, but it isn't foolproof.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:34.120
And the more human Dexter becomes, through
his relationships both at home and at work,

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:38.760
the more he exposes the innocent people around
him to the collateral damage of his targets.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:43.940
On top of that, Dexter happens to be a consummate
risk-taker, and his exploits get more and

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:46.020
more dangerous as the years go by.

00:03:46.349 --> 00:03:51.019
In season 2, there's Sergeant Doakes, the
first person outside of Dexter's family to

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.720
suspect there's something wrong with him.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.820
Doakes is killed by Dexter's ex-girlfriend,
Lila, who does it in an effort to protect

00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:58.320
him.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:04.700
What's worse at least for Doakes is that Dexter
manages to pin his own crimes on the detective,

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.800
ruining his stellar record posthumously.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.880
Nobody goes to Doakes' funeral.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:14.120
In season 3, Dexter unleashes a real monster
with District Attorney Miguel Prado.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.520
When Prado finds out who Dexter really is,
he wants to learn Harry's code.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:22.860
The code winds up meaning nothing, however,
and Prado goes on to kill a rival attorney

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.760
who was about to expose his corruption.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:31.980
By season 7, Dexter's lieutenant, Maria LaGuerta,
learns his true identity and launches an investigation

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:33.330
into Doakes' innocence.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:38.140
Ultimately, it forces Dexter's sister, Deb,
to choose between him and her colleague.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:42.060
Deb chooses her brother, but not without great
personal loss.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:47.700
But arguably the worst death that Dexter has
set in motion is that of his eventual wife,

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:48.200
Rita.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:53.900
Throughout season 4, Dexter engages in a push
and pull with Arthur Miller, a.k.a the Trinity

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:57.460
Killer, who targets victims based on their
similarities to his own family.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:02.380
Although Dexter is ultimately successful in
putting Arthur on his table, he leaves room

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:05.180
for Rita to be the last Trinity kill.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:09.500
And, in a symbolic turn of events that has
since been named one of the most shocking

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:15.020
television deaths of all time, Arthur leaves
Dexter's son, Harrison, sitting in a pool

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:19.600
of his mother's blood, just as Dexter was
when Harry found him as a child.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:25.600
Other crime shows may wait until later seasons
before really amping up the stakes, but Dexter

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:30.000
has his crimes come to light by the show's
second season, when divers find his dumping

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.660
ground off the Miami coast.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:36.960
Dubbed the Bay Harbor Butcher, Dexter's true
identity remains unknown, and because of his

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:41.600
position in the police department, he even
assists in the lab work for his own crimes.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:46.360
This tension does a great deal for Dexter's
character development right off the bat.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:51.300
Harry had taught him never to get caught,
and because of his intellect, Dexter thought

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.540
he had the system beat.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:57.630
But when his dumping ground is revealed, it's
an enormous reality check that grounds Dexter

00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:58.680
for a few years.

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:04.670
The Bay Harbor Butcher also marks a turning
point in Dexter's arc where collateral deaths

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:08.000
that don't meet the standard of Harry's code
begin in earnest.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:12.640
Dexter frames Sergeant Doakes for his murders,
although he has no intention of killing him.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:18.160
But Dexter's former lover, Lila, becomes so
obsessed with him that she's driven to kill

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:20.860
Doakes, hopeful that Dexter will love her
in return.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:25.120
She's wrong and winds up being the next Bay
Harbor Butcher victim.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:31.640
Like Hannibal Lecter, Dexter is one of the
few serial killers viewers actually root for,

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:33.900
even after he gets innocent folks killed.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:39.370
Michael C. Hall's fierce yet compassionate
performance is a big reason why Dexter feels

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:40.060
so human.

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:44.700
His internal monologue, courtesy of the Dexter
writers room, is another.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.680
But for some, Dexter's isn't just someone
to root for.

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:49.460
"People think they've found their own personal
Batman."

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:54.900
People have actually committed real-life crimes
because they felt they related to him on such

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:55.600
a deep level.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:07:00.840
Maybe the show made Dexter a little bit too
real, too sympathetic, and too relatable.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:06.520
Then again, Dexter's kill list is really,
really long, so now that we've seen the ending

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:11.430
of Dexter, we should probably be thankful
more people haven't been inspired by his laundry

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:12.430
list of crimes.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:17.920
At the beginning of the show, Dexter is convinced
that he can't be in a proper relationship

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:22.140
because physical intimacy would likely reveal
his inner monster to the other person.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:27.770
Rita seems perfect for him because as an assault
survivor, she isn't interested in the physical

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:28.500
at all.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:29.760
"She's perfect.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:33.620
Because Rita is, in her own way, as damaged
as me."

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:37.300
Eventually, however, it does become a factor
in their relationship.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:42.600
And, when Dexter joins Narcotics Anonymous
to provide a cover for his activities, he

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:47.460
gets a beautiful sponsor in Lila - and discovers
that he actually is a physical person but

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:49.580
only with people who really see him.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:55.380
Things are further complicated when Rita gets
pregnant, and Dexter feels obligated to play

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:58.780
father, both to that child and to Rita's other
kids.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:03.560
After Rita's tragic death, Dexter is sure
he'll be alone for the rest of his life, and

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:04.800
he's sort of okay with it.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:10.660
But then he meets Lumen, the Barrel Girl survivor,
and realizes that he misses having a partner

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:14.300
especially a partner who understands him as
deeply as Lila did.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:19.360
Dexter ultimately meets his match in Hannah
McKay, another serial killer who falls in

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.420
love with him, as he does with her.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:26.630
For Dexter, his experience of both love and
physical intimacy comes from the women who

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:31.120
recognize and appreciate his monstrousness
and his humanity.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:36.420
Arguably the most important woman in Dexter's
life is his adopted sister, Debra.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:42.240
Debra is Dexter's grounding force, constantly
reminding him of the good she sees in him.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:45.120
In many ways, Debra is Dexter's living conscience.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:48.320
But for Debra, the relationship is far more
complicated.

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:53.249
In season 1, she winds up in the middle of
a bloody back and forth between Dexter and

00:08:53.249 --> 00:08:58.100
his biological brother, another serial killer
known as the Ice Truck Killer.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:03.339
He kidnaps and tortures Debra in an attempt
to bond with Dexter, and the experience leaves

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:06.620
her traumatized and emotionally dependant
on her brother.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:10.980
Debra's relationship bad luck would continue
throughout the series.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:16.060
When another of her boyfriends becomes the
target of a serial killer named The Skinner,

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:18.500
the experience triggers Debra's earlier trauma.

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:24.140
She ultimately finds comfort in a much older
man and colleague, but tragically, he too

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:26.220
leaves her life when he's shot and killed.

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:32.279
Debra's shoot-from-the-hip style brings her
career highs and lows, from vice to homicide

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:33.920
detective to lieutenant.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:38.620
After she discovers her beloved brother is
a serial killer, she joins the private sector

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:39.900
as an investigator.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:44.820
Complicating things further, Debra realizes
that her feelings for Dexter are not just

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:45.860
family love.

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:50.180
She goes against everything she believes in
when she kills LaGuerta to save her brother,

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:54.760
and the experience puts her on the eventual
downward spiral that leads to her untimely

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:55.260
death.

00:09:56.020 --> 00:10:01.240
Dexter, Hannah, and his son Harrison are just
about to ride off into the Buenos Aires sunset

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:04.500
to live happily ever after when Dexter gets
sloppy again.

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:09.940
He leaves fellow serial killer Oliver Saxon
alive in order for Debra to arrest him.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:14.520
But Oliver frees himself and shoots Debra
in the stomach, severely wounding her.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:20.780
When Dexter realizes that he's the one responsible
for Debra getting shot and put on life support,

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.900
he understands that he will never have a happy
ending.

00:10:23.629 --> 00:10:28.520
He sends Hannah and Harrison to Buenos Aires
without him, takes Debra off life support,

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:29.520
and fakes his own death.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:33.760
Dexter had always worried Harrison would turn
out to be a monster like him.

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:39.040
In the end, Harrison is left to be raised
by another serial killer in another country,

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:41.180
with no idea that his father is still alive.

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:46.320
Could this be the perfect setup for a Dexter
spinoff years down the road featuring Harrison?

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:52.060
After the death of his sister, and the loss
of his son and lover, Dexter's internal monologue

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:52.600
disappears.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:56.600
By the end of Dexter's eighth and final season,
he is empty.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:01.020
He has come to terms with the fact that it's
not safe for him to be around people especially

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:03.080
not innocent people he loves.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:08.500
Lumberjack Dexter lives alone in a cabin in
the woods, which begs the question: has he

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:09.160
stopped killing?

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:14.940
He no longer has access to a police database
and can't vet victims per Harry's code.

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:20.120
But throughout the show, Dexter makes it clear
that he doesn't have a choice in killing.

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:21.940
He needs it to survive.

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:26.560
So after the end of Dexter, who and how is
he killing now?

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:31.839
The ambiguous closing shot of a bearded Dexter
silently staring into the camera certainly

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:34.220
leaves a lot of room for future seasons.

